{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b748beae-c081-4452-bf03-887775408d9e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-920d3ad43ae042d2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vy4cxq6w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigation: Workspace resolution initialization coupling in the artifacts-only server context\n\n## Description\n\nResolve whether workspace resolution in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` (and the `kubernetes://` workspace store it backs) can initialize and resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The answer determines whether the plugin extension work is verification-only or requires refactoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path, and shapes the server-side workspace-provider initialization approach.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Trace the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` workspace provider initialization path (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and identify every dependency on tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store provides experiment-to-workspace mapping that is accessible without initializing tracking stores (a strategy assumption explicitly marked \"needs validation\").\n- Determine whether artifact request paths under the artifacts API surface carry sufficient information (experiment ID / run ID) to resolve workspace membership for the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout (also a marked assumption).\n- If coupling exists, produce a concrete refactoring plan that factors workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the existing entry-point contract.\n- Deliverable: a findings report with source-level evidence and a bounded outcome classification (coupled vs. not coupled).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The findings report answers each scoping question above with an explicit determination backed by source references (files, functions, initialization call paths).\n- The outcome is classified as either (a) workspace resolution initializes without tracking stores, or (b) coupling is identified, accompanied by a refactoring plan naming the modules and functions to change.\n- If coupled, the refactoring plan preserves the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point registration mechanism, so consumers need no contract change.\n- A recommendation for the server-side workspace-provider initialization approach in artifacts-only mode is recorded for the downstream implementation work.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-7 (P1 — auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context) and, transitively, HLR-2 (P0 — workspace-validated artifact serving): the outcome determines the scope of both. No HLR is implemented directly by this investigation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":85201,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94604f82b408a2f8","agent_id":"a4d4447c1339d2689","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"031df909-82c1-4423-a8a1-571b94796b9b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:40:40.332Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
