{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3cd03f63-8819-47d7-b92b-dff27efacd78","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f25471e74d0525a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vy4cxq6w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E003.md","content":"# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n\n## Description\n\nMake the auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. This epic verifies and, if the initialization-coupling investigation finds coupling, extends the plugin so workspace resolution initializes independently and resolves workspace membership from artifact request paths.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify and, where needed, extend the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` workspace provider so its initialization does not require tracking store or model registry store initialization; if the investigation identified coupling, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin per its refactoring plan.\n- Ensure experiment-to-workspace resolution works for artifact requests: resolve artifact paths following the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure to the parent experiment's workspace assignment via the `kubernetes://` workspace store.\n- Preserve the existing `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point registration and `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading mechanism — the plugin's consumers must not need a contract change.\n- Preserve the plugin's behavior in the full tracking server context: no regression to workspace resolution for non-artifact operations.\n- Per Staff Engineer input, do not prescribe Kubernetes API authorization mechanics (such as SelfSubjectAccessReview details); reuse the existing auth plugin infrastructure, with the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup unchanged.\n- Unit tests for resolution in the artifacts-only context (stores uninitialized) and regression tests for the full-server context.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Workspace resolution initializes and resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are uninitialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n- Artifact request paths following the `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure resolve to the correct workspace assignment.\n- Existing workspace resolution behavior in the full tracking server context is unchanged (regression tests pass).\n- The `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point registration mechanism is preserved with no consumer-facing contract change.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — implemented here.\n- Enables HLR-2 (P0): workspace-validated artifact serving in the server depends on this resolution capability.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":86716,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94604f82b408a2f8","agent_id":"a4d4447c1339d2689","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"05f3ed5f-4599-437f-9eaa-d6f6f275d133","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:40:54.546Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
