{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-89ed920d-b2c4-4fdb-a09c-a92ac6b50f4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-98d42d6cfe7b0e5f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-vy4cxq6w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E006.md","content":"# Cross-component integration testing for workspace-aware artifact serving\n\n## Description\n\nBuild and run the integration and regression suite that validates the assembled split-server solution end to end: multi-tenant workspace scenarios, fail-closed behavior, single-tenant and backwards-compatibility regression, and split-server artifact traffic routing per the resolved routing design. This is the strategy's explicitly allocated integration-testing work unit, converging the server, plugin, and operator deliverables.\n\n## Scope\n\n- An automated end-to-end scenario suite, building on the existing MLflow test infrastructure, covering:\n  - multi-tenant allow/deny: a workspace member receives artifacts (HTTP 200) and a non-member is denied (HTTP 403) through the operator-deployed artifacts-only instance;\n  - fail-closed: with the workspace store unreachable, artifact requests are denied (HTTP 503) rather than served without validation;\n  - single-tenant / no-workspace-flag regression: deployments without `--enable-workspaces` retain current artifact serving behavior;\n  - backwards compatibility: existing flag combinations, API contracts, and configuration keys are unchanged;\n  - split-server routing: artifact traffic reaches the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the routing design selected by the routing investigation (gateway-level path routing or tracking-server delegation), and non-artifact traffic remains on the main tracking server.\n- Wire the suite into CI.\n- Document results against the strategy's acceptance criteria.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The automated suite covers every scenario listed in Scope and passes against the assembled split-server deployment.\n- Each of the strategy's acceptance criteria — multi-tenant allow (HTTP 200) and deny (HTTP 403), current-behavior preservation without workspace flags, fail-closed denial (HTTP 503), operator creation of the distinct artifacts-only Deployment/Service/HTTPRoute, and the artifacts-only container command flags — is exercised by the suite with recorded results.\n- Routing scenario coverage matches the routing approach that was implemented (gateway-level path routing or tracking-server delegation).\n- The suite runs in CI without manual intervention.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Verifies HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4 (P0) end to end — the P0 behaviors are implemented and unit-verified within the server work; this epic provides assembled-topology verification.\n- Verifies HLR-5, HLR-6, HLR-7 (P1) — the operator topology, artifact traffic routing, and plugin resolution in the artifacts-only context.\n- No HLR is implemented directly by this epic; its priority (P1) reflects that its distinct scope is the assembled P1 topology plus holistic regression of the P0 behaviors.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":88520,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94604f82b408a2f8","agent_id":"a4d4447c1339d2689","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"5626af5e-348f-4ec4-ad2a-751be01e2e15","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:41:21.305Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009 into epics"}
