{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c00361f6ca47548","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Workspace resolution initialization coupling in the artifacts-only\n4\t  server context'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 1\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: High\n20\tai_implementability_score: 3\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: Workspace resolution initialization coupling in the artifacts-only server context\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolve whether workspace resolution in `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` (and the `kubernetes://` workspace store it backs) can initialize and resolve experiment-to-workspace mapping in an MLflow server running in artifacts-only mode, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The answer determines whether the plugin extension work is verification-only or requires refactoring workspace resolution into an independent initialization path, and shapes the server-side workspace-provider initialization approach.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Trace the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` workspace provider initialization path (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) and identify every dependency on tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n35\t- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store provides experiment-to-workspace mapping that is accessible without initializing tracking stores (a strategy assumption explicitly marked \"needs validation\").\n36\t- Determine whether artifact request paths under the artifacts API surface carry sufficient information (experiment ID / run ID) to resolve workspace membership for the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` layout (also a marked assumption).\n37\t- If coupling exists, produce a concrete refactoring plan that factors workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the existing entry-point contract.\n38\t- Deliverable: a findings report with source-level evidence and a bounded outcome classification (coupled vs. not coupled).\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- The findings report answers each scoping question above with an explicit determination backed by source references (files, functions, initialization call paths).\n43\t- The outcome is classified as either (a) workspace resolution initializes without tracking stores, or (b) coupling is identified, accompanied by a refactoring plan naming the modules and functions to change.\n44\t- If coupled, the refactoring plan preserves the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point registration mechanism, so consumers need no contract change.\n45\t- A recommendation for the server-side workspace-provider initialization approach in artifacts-only mode is recorded for the downstream implementation work.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- Enables HLR-7 (P1 — auth plugin workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context) and, transitively, HLR-2 (P0 — workspace-validated artifact serving): the outcome determines the scope of both. No HLR is implemented directly by this investigation.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b8bc00da466fea9","agent_id":"a4770eb0e41426a63","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"b2e009d2-8ff7-4c98-997d-2f2f884102e3","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:48.139Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c00361f6ca47548","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
