{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b06fb57c6dc503b4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: Artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDecide how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance: whether gateway-level routing (Gateway API HTTPRoute path rules) suffices with no tracking server change, or whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The answer determines the HTTPRoute design for both deployments and whether server-side delegation work exists.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Analyze how artifact API traffic reaches the artifacts-only proxy today, and which routing surfaces (Gateway API HTTPRoute path/host rules, created under the operator's existing runtime CRD discovery pattern for optional dependencies) are available.\n34\t- Determine whether path-based gateway routing can direct artifact API traffic from the main tracking host to the dedicated artifacts-only instance with no tracking server configuration change.\n35\t- If gateway-level routing is insufficient, determine what tracking-server configuration would be required to delegate artifact operations to a dedicated instance (configuration surface and accepted flags/environment).\n36\t- Assess the implications for the dedicated instance's HTTPRoute and exposure design (externally path-routed vs. internal behind delegation).\n37\t- Classify the outcome as Outcome A (gateway-level routing suffices, no server change) or Outcome B (tracking-server delegation configuration required), and hand the selected branch its design.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A decision is recorded classifying the outcome as A or B, backed by evidence from the operator and server codebases and the Gateway API routing capabilities in use.\n42\t- If Outcome A: the path/host matching design is documented, including which artifact request paths must route to the dedicated instance and which traffic must remain on the main tracking server.\n43\t- If Outcome B: the required tracking-server configuration surface is identified and documented precisely enough to implement the delegation.\n44\t- The HTTPRoute/exposure design implications for the dedicated artifacts-only instance are documented.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- Enables HLR-6 (P1 — main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated instance) and informs the HTTPRoute design portion of HLR-5 (P1 — dedicated Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute). No HLR is implemented directly by this investigation.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b8bc00da466fea9","agent_id":"a4770eb0e41426a63","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"e5306f50-f6b9-4561-b11a-7351b4b0f2ae","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:48.895Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b06fb57c6dc503b4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
