{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3470e04f8d4e7eb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If workspace resolution is not coupled to tracking store initialization,\n15\t    this epic reduces to verification and regression testing of the existing resolution;\n16\t    if coupled, refactor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path\n17\t    within the plugin per the investigation's refactoring plan.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake the auth plugin's workspace resolution function correctly in the MLflow artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. This epic verifies and, if the initialization-coupling investigation finds coupling, extends the plugin so workspace resolution initializes independently and resolves workspace membership from artifact request paths.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify and, where needed, extend the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` workspace provider so its initialization does not require tracking store or model registry store initialization; if the investigation identified coupling, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin per its refactoring plan.\n44\t- Ensure experiment-to-workspace resolution works for artifact requests: resolve artifact paths following the S3-standard `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure to the parent experiment's workspace assignment via the `kubernetes://` workspace store.\n45\t- Preserve the existing `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point registration and `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading mechanism — the plugin's consumers must not need a contract change.\n46\t- Preserve the plugin's behavior in the full tracking server context: no regression to workspace resolution for non-artifact operations.\n47\t- Per Staff Engineer input, do not prescribe Kubernetes API authorization mechanics (such as SelfSubjectAccessReview details); reuse the existing auth plugin infrastructure, with the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` setup unchanged.\n48\t- Unit tests for resolution in the artifacts-only context (stores uninitialized) and regression tests for the full-server context.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Workspace resolution initializes and resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping in a server context where tracking and model registry stores are uninitialized, demonstrated by automated tests.\n53\t- Artifact request paths following the `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` structure resolve to the correct workspace assignment.\n54\t- Existing workspace resolution behavior in the full tracking server context is unchanged (regression tests pass).\n55\t- The `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry-point registration mechanism is preserved with no consumer-facing contract change.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — implemented here.\n60\t- Enables HLR-2 (P0): workspace-validated artifact serving in the server depends on this resolution capability.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b8bc00da466fea9","agent_id":"a4770eb0e41426a63","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"dce934d6-f6d6-4e7f-b6a0-0a3daaa81a53","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:51.595Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3470e04f8d4e7eb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
