{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e51a47a84d5d4d1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: The dedicated instance's HTTPRoute and exposure design changes\n15\t    with the routing outcome; if tracking-server delegation is required, main-deployment\n16\t    routing configuration is implemented in the delegation branch instead of gateway-level\n17\t    routing.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# MLflow operator dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — the split-server topology — and propagate workspace configuration to it using the same mechanisms as the main tracking deployment. Users continue to configure a single MLflow CR; the operator manages the split topology declaratively.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New Helm chart templates within the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (MLflow CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via server-side apply) for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, separate from the main tracking Deployment.\n44\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms used for the main tracking deployment; the artifacts-only container command runs `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n45\t- Create HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies; the instance's route/exposure design follows the routing design investigation's outcome.\n46\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment — the authentication layer is unchanged.\n47\t- Operator validation: reject MLflow CR configurations where split-server artifact serving is enabled but the artifacts-only instance would lack workspace flags, since misconfiguration could let artifact requests bypass workspace validation.\n48\t- Early in the epic, validate the recorded assumption that the Helm chart rendering supports adding a second Deployment without structural chart changes; if structural rework is needed, complete it within this epic before templating the instance.\n49\t- Configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment is not in this epic's scope: it is implemented per the routing design decision (gateway-level path routing, or tracking-server delegation plus its operator wiring).\n50\t- Coupling to the server capability is an acceptance-criterion gate, not a scheduling dependency: the rendered artifacts-only command must run against an MLflow server image that supports the workspace-aware artifacts-only flag combination.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Reconciling an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute distinct from the main tracking Deployment, measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n55\t- The rendered artifacts-only Deployment container command runs `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`, verified by inspecting the rendered Deployment spec.\n56\t- Workspace configuration is propagated to the artifacts-only instance through the same mechanisms as the main tracking deployment.\n57\t- HTTPRoute creation follows the existing conditional runtime CRD discovery pattern (no hard Gateway API dependency when the CRDs are absent).\n58\t- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the artifacts-only instance, configured identically to the main tracking deployment.\n59\t- The operator rejects CR configurations where the artifacts-only instance would lack workspace flags, with a clear validation error.\n60\t- Deployed against an MLflow server image supporting the workspace-aware artifacts-only flag combination, the dedicated instance serves workspace-validated artifacts.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — implemented here.\n65\t- Supports HLR-6 (P1): the routing configuration over this instance is implemented per the routing design decision and validated with the assembled topology.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b8bc00da466fea9","agent_id":"a4770eb0e41426a63","session_id":"63af744c-8e12-472e-a169-23c6bb583974","uuid":"9a1bbadb-d972-47cb-8504-40cff4245262","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:53.190Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e51a47a84d5d4d1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
